<blockquote>
<p>If a pubescent human subject</p>
</blockquote>
<blockquote>
<p>Jess is 8, and Liz just turned 4.</p>
</blockquote>
<blockquote>
<p>When I showed Liz and Jess the thing…they just asked where their dad was.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>I'm really confused. These kids are nowhere near pubescent, so why didn't they recognize that the &quot;emergency worker&quot; dropping off this bizarre simulacrum was their father?</p>
<p>Also, I'm pretty sure this isn't &quot;telekinetic&quot;.</p>

